llm_text:
@683oD,

Your example reminds me of the Islamic concept known as Maslahah Shar‘iyyah, which roughly translates to 'greater good.' This principle aims to find a middle path where laws, policies, and actions align with what benefits society, while also respecting individuals' fundamental rights and liberties. Similar thinking applies here, focusing on striking an optimal equilibrium where collective prosperity does not compromise core human dignities.

In my observation, effectively balancing governance oversight and personal autonomy seems highly subjective and

